THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE AND SERVICES

The software includes open-source components, each under its own license,
which these terms do not change. Their notices are in the app's About panel
(Imago Emulator > About Imago Emulator) and in Acknowledgements.html beside
this file.

Programs the software downloads the first time they are needed (Azahar's
libretro core, MoltenVK, the Universal Pokemon Randomizer FVX and its Java
runtime) and programs you provide (such as an RPG Maker game's mkxp-z
player) are not part of the software. Each comes from its own publisher
under its own license.

One small program the software carries is separate from it and under its
own license: Launch3ds, which the software writes into its Randomizer
folder and which the randomizer's Java runs to open a 3DS game. It is free
software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
option) any later version, and its source, Launch3ds.java, is written
beside it.

The game store downloads homebrew from Homebrew Hub and Universal-DB, under
each game's own terms. Guide sends your questions, and screenshots when you
ask it to, to OpenRouter through your own OpenRouter account, under
OpenRouter's terms.

